Package: engineering-os
Version: 0.1.0
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Depends: nodejs (>= 18)
Maintainer: Engineering OS Team <payswapdotorg@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/payswapdotorg/engineering-os
Description: Engineering OS — unified engineering collaboration platform
 A unified, open-source-first engineering workspace in which engineers across
 civil, architectural, structural, mechanical, electrical, electronic,
 industrial, computer, marine and related disciplines can collaborate with
 people and agents, operate real open-source engineering engines, and
 automate complete workflows — without manually reconstructing project
 context in every tool.
 .
 Engineering OS does not rewrite CAD, BIM or solver engines. It integrates
 existing open-source engines through a registered adapter layer, connected
 by a common project & artifact graph, a shared quantity ledger and
 estimating model, a Design Studio with a real 3D model viewer, and a
 durable workflow and agent runtime. The engines themselves (cadquery,
 IfcOpenShell, LibreOffice, …) are NOT bundled — the product detects what
 is installed on the host.
 .
 Architecture note: the payload is application JS + python adapters, but the
 bundled Prisma client ships a native linux-x64 query engine
 (libquery_engine-debian-openssl-3.0.x.so.node) and sharp ships x64 native
 bindings, so the package is amd64 — not Architecture: all. The node runtime
 itself is a dependency (nodejs >= 18), not bundled. See
 packaging/README.md for the honest reasoning record.
